    "result_text": "No dangling references. The change is complete and the full test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI consolidated the three separate duplicate checks (telephone, email, household) into a single derived `identityKey` and made it the sole duplicate-detection rule for `POST /api/owners`.\n\n**The key** \u2014 `normalizedTelephone + '|' + (email or empty) + '|' + (householdId or empty)`:\n- `src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java` \u2014 added a `@Transient getIdentityKey()` alongside the existing derived getters, so it maps to the DTO automatically and is returned in responses.\n- `src/main/resources/openapi.yml` \u2014 added the read-only `identityKey` property to the `Owner` schema (regenerates into `OwnerDto`).\n\n**The single check**:\n- New `EnsureUniqueIdentity` function rejects a create only when the new owner's **whole** `identityKey` equals an existing owner's, throwing the new checked `DuplicateIdentityException` (\u2192 409 via `DuplicateIdentityExceptionHandler`, with escalation YAML).\n- Wired into `owners.POST.yml` **after** `assignHousehold`, so the computed `householdId` is part of the key before the comparison runs.\n\n**Removed** the now-obsolete `EnsureUniqueTelephone`/`EnsureUniqueEmail`/`EnsureUniqueHousehold` functions, their three exceptions + handlers + escalation YAMLs, and their pipeline steps; tidied the stale `@link` in `AssignHousehold`.\n\n**Behaviour change verified by tests**: because telephone is part of the key, two members of the same household (same `householdId`) with different telephones now have different keys and are both allowed (Cp11, Cp23); only an exact full-key match is a duplicate (Cp03, Cp10, Cp25, Cp28). Full suite: **39 tests, 0 failures**.\n\nOne design note worth flagging: for a non-household owner `householdId` is `null` \u2192 empty segment, so the key reduces to `telephone||`. This means the household duplicate check now effectively keys on telephone for non-shared owners (matching the spec's \"whole key\" semantics), which is why the Cp10 test copies the telephone into the second owner \u2014 same lastName+address alone no longer collides.",
